        <mxCell id="note" value="Page 5 — section x language. Which topics each language skill gives its own rules file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SOLID = a file of its own. LIGHT = shares a file with another topic, or is a section inside a broader file (the cell says which). BLANK = no dedicated treatment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Four sections are universal — idioms, security, performance, tooling. The variation is not arbitrary: Errors gets a file only where the error MODEL is distinctive (Rust, Go); Typing only in the gradual-typing pair; Memory/UB only where memory is manual. sota-shell-scripting is excluded — 9 files with a different spine, grouped with languages but not a peer." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=none;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
